text:
mimi: Quick heads-up: dashboards show a tiny but persistent stream where clients set `X-API-Versions: v1 | v2` (pipe-delimited) and those requests end up routed to v1. Noticed across two critical routes.

raj: pipe? our parser only handled commas/spaces historically. we ended up falling back to v1 in those cases.

oliver: That fallback is dangerous because it silently degrades customers. We should defend the routing layer: if the header is ambiguous (multiple tokens or unknown separators) prefer the highest-supported version and surface it for ops.

mimi: Proposal: introduce an "ambiguity-shield" path. Behavior: detect multi-token or unknown-delim headers, pick preferred version (v2 if present), attach tags `ambiguous_header=true` and `shielded=true`, do not count them against per-route quota, and stream full raw header to sampled telemetry for 72h.

raj: For parsing, simple tolerant split: `tokens = raw.split(/[,;|\s]+/).filter(Boolean)` then choose prefer list `['v2','v1']`. If none matches, pick tokens[0] but mark `chosen_from_unknown=true`.

oliver: We should also keep a 100% capture for the ambiguity-shield cohort so console shows exact client ids and raw samples. Other header anomalies can be 0.5% sampled.

infra-bot: Filed INF-2612 to track ambiguity-shield: parser change, quota-exempt flag, telemetry fields, and console card.

mimi: Console asks: add a small non-modal banner on the route page when ambiguity_shield_rate > 0.3% reading "Ambiguous API headers detected Investigate headers -> link" and include a quick table: top client id, sample raw header, shareable link to PR. Ops should be able to acknowledge the banner.

ops-bot: Alert created: `ambiguous_header_shield` will page SRE if shield_rate >2% sustained 5m.

raj: Rollout plan: behind feature flag `ambiguity-shield` - start 2% of traffic for 30m, check token-cost delta and 5xx rate. If green, increase to 20% for 2h, then 100%. Rollback triggers: token-cost per request +1% or 5xx +0.3%.

oliver: One more: ensure quota service has a clear contract for `shielded=true` so we don't accidentally treat those as normal requests and throttle customers. We'll add `x-shielded: ambiguous` header so quota layer can ignore.

mimi: I'll draft the small runbook for oncall: 1) Check console card and top clients; 2) If internal proxy is top client, page infra and attach header sample; 3) If external customer dominates, hand to account team with sample and suggested mitigation; 4) If rolling 5xx or cost delta, flip flag off.

raj: Code sketch for parsing (pseudo-js):
```js
const raw = req.headers['x-api-versions'] || '';
const tokens = raw.split(/[,;|\s]+/).filter(Boolean);
if (tokens.length === 0) return defaultRoute();
const prefer = ['v2','v1'];
const chosen = prefer.find(p => tokens.includes(p)) || tokens[0];
if (tokens.length > 1 || /[;|]/.test(raw)) {
  req.tags.push('ambiguous_header');
  req.headers['x-shielded'] = 'ambiguous';
}
routeTo(chosen);
```

oliver: Telemetry fields: `ambiguous_header=true/false`, `version_tokens` (sampled list), `routing_chosen`, `shielded=true/false`, `routing_reason` in {`explicit_header`, `ambiguous_prefer`, `no_header`}.

infra-bot: INF-2612 updated with candidate proxies possibly appending versions (edge-proxy, sidecar-old).

mimi: I'll own the PR and the dashboard card. Plan to unflag and open rollout tomorrow 10:00 PST. Will post PR link here and update INF-2612.

raj: I can drive quota-service change to recognize `x-shielded` this afternoon.

ops-bot: Noted. Keeping thread as canonical. :thumbsup:
